; The clean document. Read the two `(animate …)` forms against each
; other: the same head, the same keys, and only one of them is checked.
;
;   cat examples/plugins/opaque-slot/plugin.sjon \
;       examples/plugins/opaque-slot/example.sjon | sjon validate - --no-project
;
; exits 0 with no diagnostics.

(anchor :name logo)

; At the top level `animate` is a finished form: `:target` is required
; and has to name an anchor, `:from` and `:to` are numbers, `:ease`
; defaults to `linear`. Everything here is checked.
(animate :target logo :from 0 :to 1)

; Inside `:body` the same head is unfinished and nothing is reported.
; `:target` is missing, and it is not `missing_required_key`, because
; the slot is opaque and the validator never looks.
(template :name fade
  :body (animate :from 0 :to 1))

; A body may use a vocabulary this plugin never declared. `particles`
; is not a form anywhere, and it is not `unknown_form` here.
(template :name sparkle
  :body (particles :count 200 :life 2s))

; Expansion is where the pieces meet, and it is the host's job. The
; schema checks what it can: both names below have to resolve.
(apply :template fade :target logo)

; What `sjon effective` prints for this file, in the two places that
; differ from the source:
;
;   (animate :target logo :from 0 :to 1 :ease linear)
;   (template :name fade
;     :body (animate :from 0 :to 1))
;
; The top-level animate gains its `:ease` default. The one inside the
; template does not, because the defaults overlay stops where the
; validator stops. Same head, same omitted key, one splice.
